 path and the DHT transport story. Process proposal (owner to confirm Tuesday): architect design loop (Fable via claude-cloud — her subscription resets Tuesday, or agy/argon) producing a short spec, then implementation to claude/codex/agy by capability (~4-6 days incl. tests; the file-based thin version was 2-3 days but skips dao.jing publication and custody). Also still queued from the argon gates: the module-export lift-refusal hole (lift module exports by module coordinate via host-export profiles — known-gaps row exists) as a small companion design/implementation item.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:12812:  c4-i7 — the publication c5fe3f52, the discovery/authentication 059825dc-era fix 059258dc, and the\ndocs/design/dao.space.schema.datomic.md:447:- append and durable head publication have one atomic success condition;\ndocs/design/dao.space.schema.datomic.md:448:- accepted results are emitted only after durable publication;\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-effects.md:313:attempts per publication (P), then leaves the record and answers\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-effects.md:343:caller, assert the branch above (publication reported with `:durability\ndocs/design/dao.star.md:52:**Observation order.** A fact's `ok` is publication, not the router's observation of it, so the router never classifies from a projection that may lag. Each router pass reads the ingress first, then drains its session-facts and lineage-lease cursors to `blocked`, then classifies what it read. A token reaches the ingress only through a UI projected after its fact was accepted, so a fact precedes every request that names it, and a pass that has read the request has the fact to drain. The same holds for successor ids.\ndocs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md:1001:- Linker publication and semantic scanning.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:264:  publication.** A mutable profile value (bytes, a host array) has exactly\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:273:    publication.\ndocs/desi