{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"test -f collab/1793790000000-engineer-p4-conformance-so.gpt-6-luna.findings.md && sed -n '1,180p' collab/1793790000000-engineer-p4-conformance-so.gpt-6-luna.findings.md || true\"","aggregated_output":"# P4 conformance stack overflow findings\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe focused export conformance test reproduces on a reduced stack with:\n\n```sh\nclojure -J-Xss512k -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.e2e-test \\\n  -v yang.php.antlr.e2e-test/real-lowered-ts-export-called-from-php-test\n```\n\nThe first failure was in `yang.tails/mark-tails`. After replacing the test's\nwhole-tree `postwalk` used to find `php/run-main` with an identity-aware path\nlookup, the failure moved to `yin.vm/ast->datoms-with-root` while converting\nthe composed caller AST. The failure remains with the TS donor source reduced\nto a direct arrow expression and with only its `js/make-function` node selected.\n\n## Root cause and fix\n\nThe original harness evaluated the TS donor as an operand nested inside the\nPHP caller AST. The donor source assigns its function to `globalThis`, so\nlowering that assignment brings the donor program's shared global publication\nstructure into the AST being walked for the caller. This is a composition\nerror; it is not a defect in published-export reference lowering.\n\nThe harness now evaluates the lowered donor program to completion first. That\npublishes the function cell in the VM's global table. A separate PHP AST then\nreads the named cell with `js/global-get` and projects that runtime value into\nthe PHP function or global namespace before executing the unchanged PHP\nsource. The donor AST is never nested in the caller AST. The helper locates\n`php/run-main` with identity-aware traversal, avoiding a full `postwalk` over\nshared lowered subtrees.\n\nThe focused export test and all three `real-lowered-*` tests pass at the\ndefault JVM stack. The `-J-Xss512k` focused run advances past the former walk\noverflow but still overflows later in VM datom-to-AST reconstruction during\nexecution; that is separate from the former non-terminating composition walk.\n`yang.cross-lang-test` also passes at default stack (3 tests, 5 assertions).\nThe full `bb test:sub:clj yang.php` lane was started but interrupted after it\nremained in the broad PHP e2e namespace without progress output. Kondo,\ncljstyle and `git diff --check` pass for the changed test file. No full-lane\ngreen result is claimed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
